          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The local data for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CFT"} CFT
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            allows to assign to each
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            of “possible
            = succeed "\u201D:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structures"} conformal structures
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            that have the correct behaviour (satisfy the conformal
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ward+identities"} Ward identities
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlator"} correlator
            of a CFT. This is called a space of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Bl
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bl(\Sigma)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorial
            under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %strong modular functor
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Segal89"} Segal 89
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Kriz03"} Kriz 03
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Segal04"} Segal 04, def. 5.1
          %p
            To get an actual collection of correlators one has to choose from each space of conformal blocks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Bl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bl(\Sigma)
            an element such that these choices glue under composition of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sewing+constraints"} sewing constraints
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRS-theorem+on+rational+2d+CFT"} FRS-theorem on rational 2d CFT
          %p
            Dually, under a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} CS3/WZW2
            the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+3d+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of 3d Chern-Simons theory
            for more on this.
          %h2#definition Definition
          #CategoryOfRiemannSurfaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              (“of labels”) write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_{\Phi}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surfaces"} Riemann surfaces
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circles"} circles
              labeled by elements of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+maps"} holomorphic maps
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi sewed
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to X_{sewed}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi sewed
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{sewed}
              is obtained from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sewing+constraint"} sewing
              along boundary circles carrying the same labels.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, section 4, section 5
            )
          %p
            This category, being essentially the total
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+moduli+space"} Riemann moduli space
            is naturally a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+stack"} complex analytic stack
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_\Sigma
            for the component of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            on Riemann surfaces whose underlying topological surface is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              has at least one hole (boundary component), then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(\mathcal{S}_\Sigma)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          #ModularFunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em modular functor
              is a holomorphic functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi Φ
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi sVect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \colon \mathcal{S}_\Phi \longrightarrow sVect
            %p
              (i.e. a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+stacks"} complex analytic stacks
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+moduli+space"} Riemann moduli space
              to the stack of (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"}> finite
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"}> rank
              )
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+vector+bundles"} holomorphic vector bundles
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  is
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(X \coprod Y) \simeq E(X)\otimes E(Y)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  respects sewing: if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi ϕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\phi
                  is obtained from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  by cutting along a circle and giving the same label
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \Phi
                  to both resulting boundaries, then the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mrow
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi Φ
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{\phi \in \Phi}{\oplus} E(X_\phi) \longrightarrow E(X)
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  normalization: for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = S^2
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
                  we have
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(S^1) = 1
                  (the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
                  vector space).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, def. 5.1
            )
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToGenusZeroConformalBlocks Relation to genus-zero conformal blocks
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+CFT"} rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            the modular functor is fully determined by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+sphere"} Riemann sphere
            (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %em genus=0 conformal blocks
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AndersenUeno12"} Andersen &amp; Ueno 2012
          %p
            Closely related is the statement that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+category"} braided monoidal structure
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+category"} representation category
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertex+operator+algebra"} vertex operator algebra
            is fully determined by the genus=0 conformal blocks, a statement that seems to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            (highlighted in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "modular+tensor+category#EGNO15"} EGNO 15, p. 266
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "modular+tensor+category#Runkel"} Runkel, Sec. 4.3
          %h3#central_charge_and_central_extensions Central charge and Central extensions
          %p
            Any modular functor defines a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
            of conformal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/annuli"} annuli
          %p
            These correspond precisely to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+extensions"} group extensions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Diff
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff^+(S^1)
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^\times
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, prop. 5.6
            )
          %p
            These in turn are classified by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,h) \in \mathbb{C} \times \mathbb{C}/\mathbb{Z}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, prop. 5.8
            )
          #CentralCharge.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Here in terms of standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
              terminology
            %p
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is the
                %em central charge
            %p
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalues"} eigenvalues
                of
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_0
          %h3#the_knizhnikzamolodchikovhitchin_connection The Knizhnik–Zamolodchikov-Hitchin connection
          #TheProjFlatConnection.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Given a modular functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModularFunctor"}
              and given a non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological
              labelled
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_\Sigma \to \mathcal{S}_\Sigma
              the resulting
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projectively+flat+connection"} projectively flat connection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla_\Sigma
              compatible with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sewing+constraint"} sewing operation
              of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfRiemannSurfaces"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, prop. 5.4
            , see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+equation"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov equation
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              When thinking of the modular functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              as the functor of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
              then the projectively flat connection of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheProjFlatConnection"}
              would often be called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              dually as the functor assigning
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+quantum+states"} spaces of quantum states
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
              then it would typically be called the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
              (see also
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Segal04"} Segal 04, p. 44, p. 84
          #FlatConnectionForVanishingCentralCharge.num_pro
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The connection of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheProjFlatConnection"}
              is a genuine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
              (not projective) precisely if the central charge vanishes,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = 0
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CentralCharge"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, below prop. 5.4
            )
          %h3#the_verlinde_fusion_algebra The Verlinde fusion algebra
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi,\chi,\psi \in \Phi
              three labels, write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{\phi,\chi,\psi}
              for the three-holed sphere (“pair of pants”, “trinion”) with inner circles labeled by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
              and outer circle labeled by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              a modular functor as in def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModularFunctor"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ψ
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    n_{\phi, \chi,\psi} \coloneqq dim(E(P_{\phi,\chi,\psi}))
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              of the vector space that it assigns to this surface.
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\Phi]
              on the set of labels inherits the structure of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              via
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi ψ
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ψ
                    %mi ψ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\phi,\chi) \mapsto \underset{\psi}{\sum}  n_{\phi,\chi, \psi} \psi
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+algebra"} Verlinde algebra
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, section 5, p. 36-37
            )
          %h3#TopologicalLift Deprojectivization, Cancelling of central charge, topological modular functor
          %p
            By prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FlatConnectionForVanishingCentralCharge"}
            and prop.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CentralChargeOfDeterminantLine"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a modular functor of central charge
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi Det
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde E \coloneqq E \otimes Det^{\otimes c/2}
          %p
            with a possibly fractional power of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PowerOfDeterminantLine"}
          %p To make sense of this however one needs to consistently define the fractional power. For that one needs to pass to surfaces equipped with a bit more structure.
          #RiggedSurfaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              The category of
              %em rigged surfaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat {\mathcal{S}}_\Phi
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
              of that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surfaces"} surfaces
              such that for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt 1
              it gives the universal central extension of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism+group"} diffeomorphism group
            %p
              For instance the category of surfaces equipped with a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+covering+space"} universal covering space
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              underlying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line+bundle"} determinant line bundle
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}_\Sigma
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, def. (5.10) and following
            , also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BakalovKirillov"} Bakalov-Kirillov, def. 5.7.5
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModularFunctor"}
              of central charge
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CentralCharge"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi Det
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E \coloneqq E \otimes Det^{\otimes c/2}
              is well defined on the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat S_{\phi}
              of rigged surfaces, def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RiggedSurfaces"}
          %p
            Of course if one has an extension of the diffeomorphism group by a multiple of the universal extension in def.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RiggedSurfaces"}
          #SurfacesWithAtiyah2Framing.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              The category of smooth surfaces equipped with “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+2-framing"}> Atiyah 2-framing
              ” (hence with a trivialization of the spin lift of the double of their tangent bundle) provides an extension of the diffeomorphic group of level 12.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, p. 46
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              There is a natural functor from smooth surfaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-framing"} 3-framing
              (trivialization of
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo ⊕
                      %munder
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ̲
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \Sigma\oplus \underline{\mathbb{R}}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+2-framing"} Atiyah 2-framing
              in prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SurfacesWithAtiyah2Framing"}
          %blockquote
            %p
              thanks to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"} Chris Schommer-Pries
              for highlighting this point.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#powers_of_the_determinant_line Powers of the determinant line
          #PowerOfDeterminantLine.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Det
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = Det^{\otimes n}
              be the functor which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
              to the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant+line"} determinant line
              (i.e. that of its
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laplace+operator"} Laplace operator
          %p
            Super-line, see (
            %a{:href => "#KrizLai13"}> Kriz-Lai 13
            )…
          .num_defn
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The determinant lines of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PowerOfDeterminantLine"}
              constitute precisely the modular functors, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModularFunctor"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(E(X)) = 1
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, corollary (5.17)
            )
          #CentralChargeOfDeterminantLine.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              The central charge, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CentralCharge"}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo =
                      %mi Det
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = Det
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PowerOfDeterminantLine"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (c,h ) = (-2,0)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Segal04"}> Segal 04, p.43
            )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
          %h2#properties_2 Properties
          %h3#relation_to_equivariant_elliptic_cohomology__equivariant_
            Relation to equivariant elliptic cohomology / equivariant
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
          %p
            The modular functor for
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus-1 surfaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curves"}> elliptic curves
            ) is essentially what is encoded in the universal
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            (equivariant
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} pre-quantum
            incarnation of the modular functor as a systems of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundles"} prequantum line bundles
            over Chern-Simons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            (which are
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks+of+flat+connections"} moduli stacks of flat connections
            = succeed "-process" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            by forming holomorphic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            %em
              %a{:href => "equivariant+elliptic+cohomology#InterpretationInQuantumFieldTheory"} equivariant elliptic cohomology – Idea – Interpretation in Quantum field theory
            for more on this.
